```

```suggestion

def test_linprog_maximize_from_equations():
```

(It's just another way of stating it. I I don't suppose the extra 2n operations are significant in an O(n**2) operation so what you have is a simple way of doing the operation.) The following is a (loose) demonstration of the above steps:
```python
def piv(M, i, j):
    p = M[i,j]; M = Matrix(M)
    for k in range(M.rows):
        for l in range(M.cols):
            if i != k and j != l:
                M[k,l]-=M[k,j]*M[i,l]/p
    M[i,:] /=p
    M[:,j] /=-p
    M[i,j]*=-1
    return M
```

