@oscarbenjamin, I tried implementing a fix both recursively and iteratively, but given the edge cases above, it should only collapse the nested expression when they are all of the same type (all floor or all ceiling), which would impact the simplicity of the implementation.

The simplest solution I could come up with is this iterative implementation:

```python
def collapse_nested_rounds(expr, round_function):
    numerator = expr
    denominator_final = 1
    while isinstance(expr, round_function):
        arg = expr.args[0]

        if isinstance(arg, Expr):
            numerator, denominator = arg.as_numer_denom()
            if denominator.is_integer and denominator.is_positive:
                denominator_final *= denominator
                expr = numerator

    return numerator / denominator_final
```

This function is called in the `eval` method of the `RoundFunction` class as follows:

```python
collapsed_arg = collapse_nested_rounds(arg, cls)
if collapsed_arg != arg:
