review_comment:
Various places in the codebase access to the DMP.rep attribute. In this PR a DMP might be a DMP_Python which has the `.rep` attribute as its main internal data structure or it might be a DUP_Flint which has a completely different internal structure and does not have a .rep attribute.

The `.to_list()` method will work for either DMP_Python, DUP_Flint or DMP in older versions of SymPy. I could add a property method to DUP_Python like
```python
    @property
    def rep(self):
        return self.to_list()
```
That would be a bit more backwards compatible if there is any downstream code that manipulates DMP directly.

For now I haven't added that `.rep` property and instead I have just changed all places in the codebase that access `.rep` directly so that they use `.to_list()` instead. It is not clear to me that there is much need to maintain compatibility at this level. The DMP class is very clearly internal although it is available like `Poly(x).rep.rep` which does not involve any leading underscores.

