I was thinking the same and had each of those lines tested in the version I tried to translate (without success) from Rosetta Code.

Another issue is the `round`. Python rounds away from zero. I'm not sure that this will make a difference. The HMM paper uses `\ceiling x \floor` and the translations on the (Rosetta Code page]() uses the round-away-even-and-odd-the-same sort of `round`, too. So we might need a custom `round` to handle unlimited integer size:
```python
def iround(num, den):
  # round away from 0 on tie
  if num < 0:
    return -iround(-num, den)
  w, r =divmod(num, den)
  r2 = 2*r
  if r2 < den:
    return w
  return w + 1
```

