    if len(LP) > 2 and all(isinstance(i, (list, MatrixBase)) for i in LP):
```

As a workaround (instead of a deeper fix), you could pass a custom printer to lambdify. For example, with `numpy`:
```
class CustomNumpyPrinter(sympy.printing.pycode.NumPyPrinter):
        def _print_not_supported(self, expr): 
            raise NotImplementedError()

printer = CustomNumpyPrinter({'fully_qualified_modules': False, 'inline': True, 'allow_unknown_functions': False})
try:
    lambda_func = sympy.lambdify(args, expr, modules=["numpy"], printer=printer)
except NotImplementedError:
    # Fallback to other method
```
