review_comment:
What kinds of objects are series and n here? Basic instances should have Basic args. We normally need to use sympify for this. Also we should derive any attributes from the args treating obj itself as immutable.

The standard way to do this is:
```python
    def __new__(cls, series, n):
        series = _sympify(series)
        n = _sympify(n)
        return super().__new__(cls, series, n)

    @property
    def series(self):
        return self.args[0]

    @property
    def n(self):
        return self.args[1]
```
The `Basic.__new__` method will store the arguments in `args` for us. We only define `__new__` to make sure that the object is created with the right number of arguments, to sympify them and then possibly to check the type of the args.

